# The clock authority the appliance holds while it serves, handed to the group
# that already owns the device nodes.
#
# power_dpm_force_performance_level, pp_dpm_sclk, and pp_dpm_mclk arrive owned
# by root at mode 0644, so the operating point can be stated only through a
# privileged write. The appliance states it at every launch, and a launch that
# had to reach for sudo would either prompt inside a process that has already
# forked or serve at whatever the governor chose. That is how a 2B checkpoint
# came to decode at 4.16 tok/s against the 9.46 recorded for it: the governor
# reads a decode as a low-use workload and selected 400 MHz of an 1100 MHz
# engine table.
#
# The rule gives the video group write access to those three attributes and to
# nothing else. Membership in video already carries the render node, so a
# process that can submit work to the part may now also state the states it
# runs that work at, which is the authority it was exercising through the
# governor already.
ACTION=="add|change", SUBSYSTEM=="pci", DRIVER=="amdgpu", \
  RUN+="/bin/sh -c 'for attribute in power_dpm_force_performance_level pp_dpm_sclk pp_dpm_mclk; do chgrp video /sys%p/$$attribute && chmod g+w /sys%p/$$attribute; done'"
